_10","source":"CAA GNSS radio-frequency-interference safety","url":"https://www.caa.co.uk/data-and-publications/publications/documents/content/sn-2025006/","verified":"CAA GNSS evidence is signal-, region-, aircraft-, operator-, event- and time-specific and is not an exact parcel-level aviation-incident probability.","quality_score":"3","adoption":"CAA_GNSS_RFI_GUARD_10","direct_score_input":false},{"row":91,"status":"PASS_FISHING_STABILITY_01","source":"MCA fishing-vessel stability safety","url":"https://www.gov.uk/guidance/fishing-vessel-stability","verified":"MCA identifies capsizing from inadequate stability as a major cause of fishing-vessel fatalities, particularly on smaller vessels.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"FISHING_STABILITY_01","direct_score_input":false},{"row":92,"status":"PASS_FISHING_STABILITY_02","source":"MCA fishing-vessel stability safety","url":"https://www.gov.uk/guidance/fishing-vessel-stability","verified":"A high centre of gravity and insufficient freeboard from overloading are principal causes of instability.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"FISHING_STABILITY_02","direct_score_input":false},{"row":93,"status":"PASS_FISHING_STABILITY_03","source":"MCA fishing-vessel stability safety","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/fishing-vessel-stability-guidance","verified":"MCA guidance explains stability principles, associated hazards and measures that owners, skippers and crew can take.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"FISHING_STABILITY_03","direct_score_input":false},{"row":94,"status":"PASS_FISHING_STABILITY_04","source":"MCA fishing-vessel stability safety","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-code-of-practice-for-the-safety-of-small-fishing-vessels-of-less-than-15m-length-overall/the-code-of-practice-for-the-safety-of-small-fishing-vessels-of-less-than-15m-length-overall","verified":"Vessels must maintain the required intact stability for their intended conditions of service.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"FISHING_STABILITY_04","direct_score_input":false},{"row":95,"status":"PASS_FISHING_STABILITY_05","source":"MCA fishing-vessel stability safety","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-code-of-practice-for-the-safety-of-small-fishing-vessels-of-less-than-15m-length-overall/the-code-of-practice-for-the-safety-of-small-fishing-vessels-of-less-than-15m-length-overall","verified":"Stability information should be available on board and instructions should be followed by those on watch.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"FISHING_STABILITY_05","direct_score_input":false},{"row":96,"status":"PASS_FISHING_STABILITY_06","source":"MCA fishing-vessel stability safety","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-code-of-practice-for-the-safety-of-small-fishing-vessels-of-less-than-15m-length-overall/the-code-of-practice-for-the-safety-of-small-fishing-vessels-of-less-than-15m-length-overall","verified":"Changes that add, remove or reposition significant weight require assessment of their effect on vessel stability.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"FISHING_STABILITY_06","direct_score_input":false},{"row":97,"status":"PASS_FISHING_STABILITY_07","source":"MCA fishing-vessel stability safety","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-code-of-practice-for-the-safety-of-small-fishing-vessels-of-less-than-15m-length-overall/annex-9-the-wolfson-stability-guidance-method","verified":"The Wolfson method provides colour-coded stability guidance for loading, lifting operations and limiting sea states.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"FISHING_STABILITY_07","direct_score_input":false},{"row":98,"status":"PASS_FISHING_STABILITY_08","source":"MCA fishing-vessel stability safety","url":"https://www.gov.uk/guidance/fishing-vessel-stability","verified":"Skippers should account for cranes, loose water or fish, overloading, minimum freeboard and changes in fishing method.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"FISHING_STABILITY_08","direct_score_input":false},{"row":99,"status":"PASS_WITH_FISHING_STABILITY_09","source":"MCA fishing-vessel stability safety","url":"https://www.gov.uk/guidance/fishing-vessel-stability","verified":"Fishing-vessel stability risk depends on hull, loading, freeboard, centre of gravity, gear, liquids, weather, sea state and operation.","quality_score":"3","adoption":"FISHING_STABILITY_GUARD_09","direct_score_input":false},{"row":100,"status":"PASS_WITH_FISHING_STABILITY_10","source":"MCA fishing-vessel stability safety","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/fishing-vessel-stability-guidance","verified":"MCA stability evidence is vessel-, loading-, gear-, sea-state-, crew- and time-specific and is not an exact parcel-level capsize probability.","quality_score":"3","adoption":"FISHING_STABILITY_GUARD_10","direct_score_input":false}]}